research/audit/wave5-dispatch/certifier-a6cert2-002-cex-nested-open-intervals-empty.result.json:16:  "tail": "### VERDICT — CERTIFY\n\n### WHAT I READ\n- the item, in full: `items/cex-nested-open-intervals-empty.md`\n- dependencies opened on disk: `fs-nested-open-intervals-nonempty`, `def-interval`, `cor-archimedean-reciprocal`, `lem-of-inverse-positive`, `lem-of-naturals-positive`, `thm-nested-interval-property`, `def-sequence`, `def-complete-ordered-field`, `def-ordered-field`, plus the two items named in Remarks (`ex-nested-intervals-single-point`, `cex-nested-unbounded-closed-empty`) and the page manifest `library/real-analysis/monotone-sequences-and-cauchy-completeness-examples.md` to check the fixed remark's claim\n- URLs fetched: none (the repair touched only `provenance` and `verification`, and one internal wikilink; it added no new `sources.references` URL)\n\n### ASSESSMENT\n\n**The repair's two substantive content changes, checked:**\n\n1. **Dropped fact `[L5]` (nested-interval property for closed intervals).** Confirmed dead: in the pre-repair text it was cited by neither proof step (both 1.1 and 4.1 cited only `L1`/old-`L6`). Its removal is a clean simplification with no loss.\n\n2. **Replaced \"that computation is the preceding example on this page\" with a direct link `[[ex-nested-intervals-single-point]]`.** I checked this against the actual page manifest (`monotone-sequences-and-cauchy-completeness-examples.md`, lines 6-13): the two items are on the same page, but `ex-nested-intervals-single-point` is **not** the immediately preceding entry — three other items (`ex-two-subsequential-limits`, `ex-contractive-sequence-fixed-point`, `cex-cauchy-rationals-no-rational-limit`) sit between them in the manifest's reading order. The pre-repair claim was therefore false, exactly the class of Remark-adjacency defect this audit wave is tuned to find. The replacement wikilink makes no ordering claim and is accurate: I opened `ex-nested-intervals-single-point.md` and confirmed it computes $\\bigcap[0,1/k] = \\{0\\}$ as described.\n\n**Proof body (steps 1.1-4.1), unchanged by the repair but re-checked as required:** the reductio is valid — assume $x$ lies in every $J_j$, use the reciprocal Archimedean property (`cor-archimedean-reciprocal`, quoted verbatim in `[L3]`) to find $n\\ge1$ with $1/n<x$, re-index $n=j+1$, derive both $x<1/n$ and $1/n<x$, contradicting trichotomy. Every `[F#]`/`[L#]` fact I checked against its cited dependency reproduces that dependency's exact statement (hypotheses, direction, conclusion) with no inflation.\n\n**Title vs. proof:** \"The nested open intervals $(0,1/k)$ have empty intersection\" is exactly what steps 1.1-4.1 establish — no overclaim.\n\n**Cross-checked Remarks against their targets:** the \"hypothesis missing\" and \"candidate point excluded\" remarks match `thm-nested-interval-property` and `def-interval`; the boundedness remark's cross-reference to `cex-nested-unbounded-closed-empty` matches that item's actual content (closed, unbounded, empty intersection).\n\nNo new URL was introduced by this repair, so nothing needed fetching.\n\n0 fatal, 0 nonfatal"
